-- title:
--   Spreading a base-local isomorphism from a semilocalisation to a localisation
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} S$ a morphism of schemes satisfying `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle`, i.e. $f$ is smooth and proper, each fibre $f^{-1}(s)$ is connected, and $f$ carries a relative group law (a functorial group structure on the $T$-points over $\operatorname{Spec} S$, for all $S$-schemes $T$). Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime of $S$, let $g_1 \notin \mathfrak p$, let $C$ be a commutative ring that is an algebra over both $S$ and $S_{g_1} = \operatorname{Localization.Away} g_1$ compatibly, and module-finite over $S_{g_1}$; let $C_0$ be an $S$- and $C$-algebra (compatibly) which is the localisation of $C$ at the submonoid generated by the image of $S \setminus \mathfrak p$; let $r \notin \mathfrak p$ and let $X$ be an $S$- and $C$-algebra (compatibly) which is the localisation of $C$ at the image of the powers of $r$. Let $N, P$ be modules on the pullback $A_X = A \times_{\operatorname{Spec} S} \operatorname{Spec} X$, both invertible in the sense that every point has an open neighbourhood on whose preimage the module becomes isomorphic to the unit module. Let $\varphi : X \to C_0$ be a ring homomorphism over $C$, and let $\kappa : A_{C_0} \to A_X$ be a morphism commuting with the first projections to $A$ and satisfying $\kappa$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} X$ equals the projection $A_{C_0} \to \operatorname{Spec} C_0$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec} \varphi$. Assume $\kappa^* N$ and $\kappa^* P$ are isomorphic locally on the base $\operatorname{Spec} C_0$, that is, every point of $\operatorname{Spec} C_0$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ such that the restrictions of $\kappa^* N$ and $\kappa^* P$ to the preimage of $U$ in $A_{C_0}$ are isomorphic. Then there exists $r' \in S \setminus \mathfrak p$ such that for every commutative ring $Y$ that is an $S$- and $C$-algebra (compatibly) in which the image of $rr'$ is a unit, every ring homomorphism $\psi : X \to Y$ over $C$, and every $\rho : A_Y \to A_X$ compatible with the projections to $A$ and satisfying the analogous identity over $\operatorname{Spec}\psi$, the modules $\rho^* N$ and $\rho^* P$ are isomorphic locally on the base $\operatorname{Spec} Y$.
--
--   This is the law-free spreading step in the construction of polarisations over a base: an isomorphism of invertible modules valid locally on the semilocalisation $\operatorname{Spec} C_0$ of $C$ at the primes above $\mathfrak p$ is propagated to all sufficiently small localisations, uniformly in the target algebra $Y$ and the chosen map $\rho$. It is used by the corresponding statement for symmetric line bundles attached to an abelian scheme, [`GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_not_mem_forall_isLocalization_powers_mul_isSymmetric_locIsoOnBase_pullback_of_isLocalization_primeCompl`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_not_mem_forall_isLocalization_powers_mul_isSymmetric_locIsoOnBase_pullback_of_isLocalization_primeCompl).
